Subject: [PATCH 4/9] Comments that said every agreement covers the US and
 leaves voice-over out now say it was so until 2026-10-25

The review found five comments beside lines this branch changed still saying, in the present tense, what the change had
made false: the Module 5 productions' note that voice-over is outside an agent's agreement, above four parts whose access
the branch opened to an agent; Harbor Line's note that no agent is owed commission on it, which an agreement with work
abroad added now is; the pay's header and COVERED_MEDIA giving one US scope for every agreement; and inScope calling the
agency's own department "his" when its new voice-over agent's is another. Each now says what held until 2026-10-25 and
what each agreement's own terms (coveredUnder) decide from then. Comments only: no behaviour changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HBdcuKzBBMbipfFQSByALG
